    "created_at": "2026-10-20T08:49:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-20T08:49:17Z",
    "body": "A developer data point in support of this, since most of the thread is from the implementer side.\n\nWe build an internal sales CRM that runs as an installed web app and handles customer calls over WebRTC. Push delivery is no longer the problem — on Android, desktop and iOS 16.4+ the alert arrives within a couple of seconds, even with the app closed. The problem is that it arrives as an ordinary notification: one short sound, so reps miss calls. Today we fake it by re-sending the notification every few seconds while the caller waits, which is the kind of workaround this proposal would remove.\n\nTwo things matter most to us from the explainer: an associated ringtone that keeps sounding until the call is answered or dismissed, and Answer/Decline actions. Keeping it to installed web apps with explicit permission seems right to us.\n\nMobile matters as much as desktop here — the phone in a salesperson's pocket is where calls get missed. We have already added `scenario: \"incoming-call\"` to our notifications so they pick this up as soon as a browser supports it, and we would be glad to test early implementations. Thank you for pushing this forward.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
