    "updated_at": "2026-10-22T15:15:44Z",
    "body": "How would a dismissed call by the caller be represented in this API? Push is specified as it MUST show a notification, so it can't be used to dismiss the notification. But maybe Declarative Web Push can be extended for notification closure (in a way that a closure can't be `mutable` and thus cannot be abused)?\n\nFiled https://github.com/w3c/push-api/issues/427",
